 tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">03</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Chinnamastā</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">चिन्नमस्ता</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of self-sacrifice / feeding others from your own life-force</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Agni (Fire)</span><span>·</span><span>Agni<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"bhuvaneshvari\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/bhuvaneshvari-submerged\" alt=\"Bhuvaneśvarī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">04</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhuvaneśvarī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">भुवनेश्वरी</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of control / cosmic-sovereignty wound</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Prithvi (Earth)</span><span>·</span><span>Jal<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"shodashi\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/shodashi-sri-yantra\" alt=\"Ṣoḍaśī / Tripurasundarī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">05</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Ṣoḍaśī / Tripurasundarī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">षोडशी / त्रिपुरसुन्दरी</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of beauty-as-avoidance</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Agni (Fire)</span><span>·</span><span>Jal<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>3<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"bhairavi\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/bhairavi-chamber\" alt=\"Bhairavī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">06</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhairavī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">भैरवी</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of refusing the teacher</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Agni (Fire)</span><span>·</span><span>Agni<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>2<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"dhumavati\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/dhumavati-ruin\" alt=\"Dhūmāvatī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">07</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Dhūmāvatī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">धूमावती</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of inauspiciousness / widowhood-of-the-soul</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Vayu (Air)</span><span>·</span><span>Jal<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"bagalamukhi\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/bagalamukhi-pathway\" alt=\"Bagalāmukhī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">08</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bagalāmukhī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">बगलामुखी</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of being silenced / needing to freeze a hostile force</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Prithvi (Earth)</span><span>·</span><span>Agni<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>2<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"matangi\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/matangi-cremation\" alt=\"Mātaṅgī\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">09</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Mātaṅgī</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">मातङ्गी</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of transgressive voice / the outcaste within</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Vayu (Air)</span><span>·</span><span>Jal<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div><div id=\"kamala\" class=\"relative\"><button class=\"w-full text-left glass-chip overflow-hidden group transition-all duration-500 \"><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\"><div class=\"relative md:w-48 h-40 md:h-auto shrink-0 overflow-hidden\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/b9oo5abp/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920,c_limit/kalki-mirror/tantra/archetypes/kamala-observatory\" alt=\"Kamalā\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity duration-700\" style=\"filter:contrast(1.08) saturate(0.9) brightness(0.95) sepia(0.08)\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-deep-black/80 hidden md:block\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-deep-black/80 to-transparent md:hidden\"></div><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/60\">10</span></div></div><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-3\"><div><h3 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kamalā</h3><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.12em] mt-1\">कमला</p></div><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.08em] mb-3 italic\">The loop of prosperity-without-integration</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-[0.75rem] font-mono text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\"><span>Jal (Water)</span><span>·</span><span>Jal<!-- --> TIER</span><span>·</span><span>1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></button></div></div><div class=\"divider-gold mb-16\"></div><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">Supplementary Archetypes</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-foreground font-light tracking-[0.06em] engraved-heading mb-12\">Beyond the Ten</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div id=\"shaiva-ascetic\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Pāśupata Ascetic</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">पाशुपत</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of extreme asceticism as identity</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Pāśupata archetype governs the loop where self-denial becomes the self. The practitioner identifies so completely with discipline, renunciation, or rigor that the discipline itself becomes the ego-structure it was meant to dissolve. Originating in the Pāśupata Sūtras of Lakulīśa (c. 2nd c. CE), this is the oldest surviving Śaiva ascetic path — and its paradox is built into the methodology: the practitioner must act as if mad, as if possessed, deliberately attracting contempt to dissolve the social self. When this becomes performance rather than transformation, the loop is complete.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Agni (Fire)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div><div id=\"nath-alchemical\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Nāth Alchemist</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">नाथ</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of collecting techniques without embodiment</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Nāth archetype governs the loop of tantric consumerism — the practitioner who collects kuṇḍalinī techniques, cakra visualizations, and nāḍī mappings without ever sitting still long enough for the body to integrate any of it. Originating with Matsyendranāth (c. 9th-10th c. CE) and the Kaulajñānanirṇaya, the Nāth tradition is the foundation of Haṭha Yoga. But its core teaching is direct embodiment, not textual accumulation. The practitioner caught in the Nāth loop knows more about the cakras than they have ever directly experienced.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Vayu (Air)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div><div id=\"buddhist-vajra\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Vajrayoginī / Vajravārāhī</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">वज्रयोगिनी</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of sacred madness / bypass through bliss</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Vajrayoginī archetype governs the loop where the practitioner uses the intensity of tantric experience — bliss, vision, energetic phenomenon — as a bypass for the slower, less glamorous work of psychological integration. Originating in the Cakrasaṃvara cycle of Buddhist mother-tantras, Vajrayoginī is the adamantine ḍākinī who dances in the charnel ground of the mind. The practitioner caught in her loop chases peak experiences while avoiding the valleys. The teaching is that the charnel ground is not a destination but the ground on which all experience stands.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Akasha (Ether)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div><div id=\"atharvana-protective\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Pratyaṅgirā</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">प्रत्यङ्गिरा</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of hypervigilance / armor as identity</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Pratyaṅgirā archetype governs the loop where protective awareness calcifies into permanent hypervigilance — the practitioner who cannot stop scanning for threat, who has made defense into identity. Pratyaṅgirā is the Atharvaṇa protective goddess invoked to neutralise hostile force. But her loop is the confusion between protection and imprisonment: the armor that once saved you now prevents you from feeling anything at all. The teaching is that true protection is not the absence of vulnerability but the capacity to remain open within it.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Agni (Fire)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div><div id=\"shatkarma-destruction\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Ṣaṭ-karma (Destructive)</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">षट्कर्म</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of adversarial thinking / the enemy-making mind</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Ṣaṭ-karma archetype governs the loop of adversarial cognition — the practitioner who sees the world through the lens of enemy and ally, who needs opposition to define themselves, who has made conflict into a spiritual technology. The six ṣaṭ-karmas (śānti, vaśīkaraṇa, stambhana, vidveṣaṇa, uccāṭana, māraṇa) form a complete taxonomy of force applied to the external world. When internalized, they become the six ways the mind wages war on its own experience. This archetype is SEALED — documented as heritage, never operationalized.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Prithvi (Earth)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">6<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div><div id=\"preta-field\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6 h-full\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-foreground font-light\">Preta-Siddhi Field</h3><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span></div><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim tracking-[0.1em] mb-3\">प्रेतसिद्धि</p><p class=\"text-sm text-copper font-mono tracking-[0.06em] mb-4 italic line-clamp-2\">The loop of unfinished grief / the unburied dead within</p><p class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Preta archetype governs the loop of unresolved relationship with the dead — literal or symbolic. The practitioner who cannot release the past, who carries the unburied grief of ancestors, broken lineages, or unspoken family secrets. The preta-saṁvāda rite (spirit dialogue) is documented in Aghora/Kaula field manuals as a complete operational protocol for invoking, questioning, and releasing a preta. This archetype is SEALED — documented as heritage scholarship, never operationalized. The teaching is that what remains unacknowledged does not disappear; it becomes a hidden driver of behavior.</p><div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gold/5 flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">Vayu (Air)</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted\">·</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted tracking-[0.1em]\">1<!-- --> FOLIOS</span></div></div></div></div></div></div><!--$--><!--/$--></div><script>$RB=[];$RV=function(a){$RT=performance.now();for(var b=0;b<a.length;